## Permanent behavior / authority

- execution accepts exactly one explicit candidate already present by reference in the supplied eligibility result and exactly one explicit `WindowsMutationRequest`;
- preflight independently rechecks `Active`, `High`, exact capturable `TelemetryWorkloadTarget`, stable GameId match and `ActionSafety.LiveSafe`;
- typed before evidence is mandatory before mutation;
- `SystemOptimizationTransactionEngine.BeginSessionAsync()` remains the sole snapshot/apply/verify/ownership/rollback authority;
- `PerformanceCaptureCoordinator.CaptureWorkloadTypedAsync()` remains the typed before/after measurement seam on the exact same workload target;
- outcome semantics are injected through `IGenericGuardianSessionCanaryOutcomeEvaluator`; the executor defines no universal threshold;
- only `Improved` keeps the mutation active;
- `Regressive`, `Inconclusive`, unavailable after evidence, post-apply capture/evaluator failure or cancellation restore exact prior state before returning/throwing;
- cleanup after mutation is active uses `CancellationToken.None` so caller cancellation cannot skip restoration;
- kept state is session-only and exposed through `GenericGuardianSessionCanaryLease`; lease restore/dispose delegates to the proven transaction engine;
- transaction-engine durable snapshot/History behavior remains intact;
- no extra Guardian Knowledge/History persistence is added by this slice;
- no Global Controlled Benchmark Lease is acquired by live Guardian canary execution; controlled benchmark operations keep their existing lease/suspend/reconcile authority.

## Explicitly not included

- family-specific definitions of improvement;
- cooldown or Action Budget;
- runtime/application host wiring;
- learned ranking/action reliability (Track 6 item 4);
- post-session queue (item 5);
- persistent optimization/recommendation authority;
- profile/winner/ValidatedEvidence authority;
- WPF/startup/discovery changes;
- changes to specialized BlueStacks/FF Guardian behavior.

## Next gate

This documentary checkpoint must receive exact Windows CI before the next implementation slice begins. Item 3 remains open; next bounded slice is family-specific canary outcome policy using only capability-honest typed evidence, followed later by cooldown/Action Budget and runtime host wiring.
